WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.190
In March 2024, a public-sector agency moved four hundred and twelve staff to a new building.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.720
Each had a day to fill a fixed number of crates.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:15.340
57 crates had been packed for the 2017 relocation and not opened since,

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.520
and they went to the new building with the rest.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.210
Hedvig Anyanwu's doctoral thesis asks where a workplace forms its priorities.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.300
In its plans,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.320
or in its crates?

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.020
I followed four office moves at three organisations.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:33.670
On packing day, I logged almost twenty-two thousand items as they went in.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.930
When a lid wouldn't close, people gave up what they were using.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.500
They held on to material from programs that had already ended.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.310
Fourteen months later, the agency moved again.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.170
A hundred and eighteen crates went across unopened,

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.240
fifty-five of them from 2017.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.820
At the end of my fieldwork, I was allowed to open ninety-four carried-forward crates.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:02.140
Thirty-six per cent of what was inside came from programs and projects the organisation had formally ended.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.490
Nearly three times the share on packing day.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.980
Work in current use was down to four per cent.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.160
From 2027, the School of Emergent Priorities sets its own priorities this way.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.710
Each unit packs its priorities into two crates.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.890
A crate it doesn't open is carried forward,

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.160
as a standing priority.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.740
What fits under the lid is what the organisation goes on doing,

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.290
whatever its register of priorities records.
